{number: 139}
{title: More Love to Thee, O Christ}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] More love to Thee, O Christ,
[F] More love to [C] Thee!
Hear Thou the prayer I make
On [G7] bended [C] knee;
This is my earnest plea:
[F] More love, O [C] Christ, to Thee,
[F] More love to [C] Thee,
[G7] More love to [C] Thee!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Once earthly joy I craved,
[F] Sought peace and [C] rest;
Now Thee alone I seek,
Give [G7] what is [C] best;
This all my prayer shall be:
[F] More love, O [C] Christ, to Thee,
[F] More love to [C] Thee,
[G7] More love to [C] Thee!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Let sorrow do its work,
[F] Send grief and [C] pain;
Sweet are Thy messengers,
Sweet [G7] their re-[C] frain,
When they can sing with me:
[F] More love, O [C] Christ, to Thee,
[F] More love to [C] Thee,
[G7] More love to [C] Thee!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Then [C] shall my latest breath
[F] Whisper Thy [C] praise;
This be the parting cry
My [G7] heart shall [C] raise;
This still its prayer shall be:
[F] More love, O [C] Christ, to Thee,
[F] More love to [C] Thee,
[G7] More love to [C] Thee!
{end_of_verse}
